<h3 id="13-key-architectural-decisions">1.3 Key Architectural
Decisions</h3>
<p><strong>Authentication</strong>: Use the Rails 8.1 built-in
authentication generator
(<code>bin/rails generate authentication</code>) instead of Devise. This
creates <code>User</code> and <code>Session</code> models,
<code>SessionsController</code>, <code>PasswordsController</code>, and
the <code>Authentication</code> concern with
<code>require_authentication</code> and
<code>allow_unauthenticated_access</code> helpers. Simpler, fewer
dependencies, well-integrated with Rails 8.1.</p>
<p><strong>Image Storage</strong>: Use the <code>cloudinary</code> gem
directly with a custom <code>Image</code> model rather than Active
Storage with a Cloudinary adapter. Rationale:</p>
<ul>
<li>The admin must browse and select from <em>previously uploaded</em>
images when associating them with events or assigning them to galleries.
Active Storage is designed around attaching blobs to specific records on
upload, not for maintaining a persistent, browsable media library.</li>
<li>A custom <code>Image</code> model stores the Cloudinary
<code>public_id</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>width</code>,
<code>height</code>, <code>format</code>, and <code>bytes</code>,
allowing queries, thumbnails, and gallery ordering without
round-tripping to the Cloudinary API.</li>
<li>Direct use of the <code>cloudinary</code> gem gives full access to
Cloudinary's URL-based transformation API.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Event Categories</strong>: Implemented as a string column
with a constant-based inclusion validation on the <code>Event</code>
model. The fixed set (Education, Fellowship, Meetings, Community
Service) is defined as a constant. No separate <code>Category</code>
model. String values are more readable in queries and the database than
integer enums.</p>
<p><strong>Calendar</strong>: Server-rendered monthly grid using
Tailwind CSS utility classes, with Turbo Frame wrapping for
month-to-month navigation without full page reloads. No JavaScript
calendar library.</p>
<p><strong>Drag-and-Drop Reordering</strong>: SortableJS loaded via
import map, wrapped in a Stimulus controller. Gallery image positions
are persisted via a <code>position</code> integer column on the
<code>GalleryImage</code> join model.</p>
