<li><code>email</code>: format (email regex), allow blank, length
(maximum: 255)</li>
<li><code>phone</code>: format (digits, dashes, parentheses, spaces),
allow blank, length (maximum: 20)</li>
<li><code>state</code>: length (is: 2), allow blank</li>
<li><code>zip_code</code>: format (<code>/\A\d{5}(-\d{4})?\z/</code>),
allow blank</li>
<li><code>date_of_birth</code>: must be in the past if present (custom
validation)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Scopes:</strong></p>
<pre class="ruby"><code>scope :alphabetical, -&gt; { order(last_name: :asc, first_name: :asc) }
scope :birthdays_this_month, -&gt; {
  where(&quot;EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_of_birth) = ?&quot;, Date.current.month)
    .order(Arel.sql(&quot;EXTRACT(DAY FROM date_of_birth) ASC&quot;))
}</code></pre>
<p><strong>Instance Methods:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><code>full_name</code> -- returns
<code>"#{first_name} #{last_name}"</code></li>
<li><code>birthday_display</code> -- returns month and day with ordinal
formatting (e.g., "January 15th")</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2 id="3-authentication--authorization">3. Authentication &amp;
Authorization</h2>
<h3 id="31-authentication-generator">3.1 Authentication Generator</h3>
<p>Run <code>bin/rails generate authentication</code> which
produces:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>app/models/user.rb</code> -- User model with
<code>has_secure_password</code></li>
<li><code>app/models/session.rb</code> -- Session model</li>
<li><code>app/models/current.rb</code> -- <code>Current</code> singleton
(<code>Current.user</code>, <code>Current.session</code>)</li>
<li><code>app/controllers/sessions_controller.rb</code> --
Login/logout</li>
<li><code>app/controllers/passwords_controller.rb</code> -- Password
reset flow</li>
<li><code>app/controllers/concerns/authentication.rb</code> -- The
<code>Authentication</code> concern</li>
<li>Migration files for <code>users</code> and
<code>sessions</code></li>
<li>View templates for login and password reset</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Prerequisite:</strong> Uncomment
<code>gem "bcrypt", "~&gt; 3.1.7"</code> in the Gemfile and run
<code>bundle install</code> before running the generator.</p>
<h3 id="32-how-it-works">3.2 How It Works</h3>
<p>The <code>Authentication</code> concern mixed into
<code>ApplicationController</code> provides:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>require_authentication</code> -- a <code>before_action</code>
that redirects unauthenticated users to the login page. All actions
require authentication by default.</li>
<li><code>allow_unauthenticated_access</code> -- a class-level method
that skips the auth check for specified actions.</li>
<li><code>authenticated?</code> -- a boolean helper for conditional
rendering in views.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="33-authorization-strategy">3.3 Authorization Strategy</h3>
<p>Binary model: logged in = admin, not logged in = public visitor. No
roles needed.</p>
<p><strong>Controller-level pattern:</strong></p>
<pre class="ruby"><code># Mixed public/admin (e.g., EventsController):
class EventsController &lt; ApplicationController
  allow_unauthenticated_access only: [:index, :show]
end

# Admin-only (e.g., MembersController):
class MembersController &lt; ApplicationController
  # All actions require auth by default
end</code></pre>
<p><strong>View-level pattern:</strong></p>
<pre class="erb"><code>&lt;% if authenticated? %&gt;
  &lt;%= link_to &quot;Edit&quot;, edit_event_path(@event) %&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>
<h3 id="34-initial-admin-user">3.4 Initial Admin User</h3>
<p>Created via seed data in <code>db/seeds.rb</code>:</p>
<pre class="ruby"><code>User.find_or_create_by!(email_address: &quot;admin@example.com&quot;) do |user|
  user.password = &quot;changeme123&quot;
  user.password_confirmation = &quot;changeme123&quot;
end</code></pre>
<hr />
<h2 id="4-routes">4. Routes</h2>
<pre class="ruby"><code>Rails.application.routes.draw do
  # Authentication (generated)
  resource  :session,   only: [:new, :create, :destroy]
  resources :passwords, param: :token, only: [:new, :create, :edit, :update]

  # Events (public index/show, admin CRUD)
  resources :events

  # Galleries (public index/show, admin CRUD + reorder)
  resources :galleries do
    patch :reorder, on: :member
  end

  # Calendar (public)
  get &quot;calendar&quot;, to: &quot;calendar#show&quot;, as: :calendar

  # Members (admin only)
  resources :members

  # Image management (admin only)
  namespace :admin do
    resources :images, only: [:index, :new, :create, :destroy]
  end

  # Homepage
  root &quot;pages#home&quot;

  # Health check (existing)
  get &quot;up&quot; =&gt; &quot;rails/health#show&quot;, as: :rails_health_check
end</code></pre>
