<h2 id="7-image-management----cloudinary-integration">7. Image
Management -- Cloudinary Integration</h2>
<h3 id="71-gem-setup">7.1 Gem Setup</h3>
<p>Add to Gemfile:</p>
<pre class="ruby"><code>gem &quot;cloudinary&quot;, &quot;~&gt; 2.0&quot;</code></pre>
<h3 id="72-configuration">7.2 Configuration</h3>
<p><strong>Initializer</strong>
(<code>config/initializers/cloudinary.rb</code>):</p>
<pre class="ruby"><code>Cloudinary.config do |config|
  config.cloud_name = Rails.application.credentials.dig(:cloudinary, :cloud_name)
  config.api_key    = Rails.application.credentials.dig(:cloudinary, :api_key)
  config.api_secret = Rails.application.credentials.dig(:cloudinary, :api_secret)
  config.secure     = true
end</code></pre>
<p><strong>Rails credentials</strong>
(<code>bin/rails credentials:edit</code>):</p>
<pre class="yaml"><code>cloudinary:
  cloud_name: your_cloud_name
  api_key: &#39;123456789012345&#39;
  api_secret: &#39;abcdefghijklmnop&#39;</code></pre>
<h3 id="73-upload-flow">7.3 Upload Flow</h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>Admin navigates to <code>/admin/images/new</code></li>
<li>Admin selects a file via standard file input</li>
<li>Form submits to <code>Admin::ImagesController#create</code></li>
<li>Controller calls
<code>Cloudinary::Uploader.upload(params[:file], folder: "wbr-pres-cms", resource_type: "image", allowed_formats: %w[jpg jpeg png webp gif])</code></li>
<li>Cloudinary returns metadata: <code>public_id</code>,
<code>secure_url</code>, <code>width</code>, <code>height</code>,
<code>format</code>, <code>bytes</code></li>
<li>Controller creates <code>Image</code> record with these
attributes</li>
<li>Redirect to <code>admin_images_path</code> with success flash</li>
</ol>
<h3 id="74-image-deletion">7.4 Image Deletion</h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>Check if image is assigned to any events -- warn if so</li>
<li>Call
<code>Cloudinary::Uploader.destroy(image.cloudinary_public_id)</code></li>
<li>Delete <code>Image</code> record (cascades to
<code>gallery_images</code>; nullifies
<code>events.image_id</code>)</li>
